                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b1a27275-bb08-4822-b354-dec516905130",
                        "source_entry_id": "347b3608-d799-38b5-a0ab-ef94af53dd1c",
                        "source_sense_id": "6c7f9218-2585-3bb1-9829-56c0d2a0808e",
                        "source_sense_description": "bij de geboorte verkregen eigenschappen",
                        "target_lang_word": "innate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "innate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9a629241-a885-3716-ad82-805292cd2eae",
                                        "entry_id": "d3b9aff9-ec19-3549-9ba2-748bc963d1b9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Inborn; existing or having existed since birth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "647d0c0f-14cb-43c7-a654-9cd5504bbf06",
                                                "sense_id": "9a629241-a885-3716-ad82-805292cd2eae",
                                                "text": "Ironically, given France's innate reluctance to permit competition at home, the first breach in Renfe's monopoly came from SNCF offshoot Ouigo España in 2021."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "20397c68-b63f-345f-a43a-d1f0792ed134",
                                        "entry_id": "d3b9aff9-ec19-3549-9ba2-748bc963d1b9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Originating in, or derived from, the constitution of the intellect, as opposed to acquired from experience."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a9c761d-e57b-417b-acc7-23a42e51c927",
                                                "sense_id": "20397c68-b63f-345f-a43a-d1f0792ed134",
                                                "text": "innate ideas"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81c22f70-efa5-4927-b9dd-2613b6b6f7c5",
                                                "sense_id": "20397c68-b63f-345f-a43a-d1f0792ed134",
                                                "text": "There is an innate light in every man, discovering to him the first lines of duty, in the common notions of good and evil, which, by cultivation and improvement, may be advanced to higher and brighter discoveries."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8f413ea-6fb1-4349-a8e2-718f29469518",
                                                "sense_id": "20397c68-b63f-345f-a43a-d1f0792ed134",
                                                "text": "It would be ſufficient to convince unprejudiced Readers of the falſeneſs of this Suppoſition, if I ſhould only ſhew (as I hope I ſhall in the following Parts of this Diſcourſe) how Men barely by the Uſe of their natural Faculties, may attain to all the Knowledge that they have, without the help of any innate Impreſſions[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "873f8c25-3e3f-342b-ac4c-838516722516",
                                        "entry_id": "d3b9aff9-ec19-3549-9ba2-748bc963d1b9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Instinctive; coming from instinct."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1322f378-fdf1-4fa2-b09d-b965d39c3fe0",
                                                "sense_id": "873f8c25-3e3f-342b-ac4c-838516722516",
                                                "text": "Perhaps, from an innate desire of justification, sorrow always exaggerates itself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0295164-93c3-42ae-b15f-a0ecfd45ba70",
                                                "sense_id": "873f8c25-3e3f-342b-ac4c-838516722516",
                                                "text": "As if she held the clue to something secret in his breast, of the nature of which he was hardly informed himself. As if she had an innate knowledge of one jarring and discordant string within him, and her very breath could sound it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "efed5f15-9197-32db-b300-eec870322220",
                                        "entry_id": "d3b9aff9-ec19-3549-9ba2-748bc963d1b9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Joined by the base to the very tip of a filament."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40b8aad2-d8ea-4bdc-a71f-62ba5a62e71d",
                                                "sense_id": "efed5f15-9197-32db-b300-eec870322220",
                                                "text": "an innate anther"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "innate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ec565a82-6e94-3b83-99fb-591a0d4b689d",
                                        "entry_id": "58feba55-0daa-3a19-b603-0104323a9401",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cause to exist; to call into being."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a35c0899-8798-4c0a-be02-1b8c0c5f21f3",
                                                "sense_id": "ec565a82-6e94-3b83-99fb-591a0d4b689d",
                                                "text": "I never ſaw a foole leane : the chub-fac’d fop / Shines ſleek with full cramm’d fat of happineſſe, / VVhilſt ſtudious contemplation ſucks the juice / From wiſards cheekes : who making curious ſearch / For Natures ſecrets, the firſt innating cauſe / Laughs them to ſcorne, as man doth buſy Apes / VVhen they will zany men."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe3696fa-a18a-4059-95da-e3a4466c7e5e",
                                                "sense_id": "ec565a82-6e94-3b83-99fb-591a0d4b689d",
                                                "text": "[…]but the innating matter works not upon the dull matter, as upon a new material, for the innate matter is mixt with the dull part of matter[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34dab25b-eaad-431a-8e78-15cbf2c463c5",
                                                "sense_id": "ec565a82-6e94-3b83-99fb-591a0d4b689d",
                                                "text": "Here you may behold how each County is innated with a particular Genius, inclining the Natives thereof to be dextrous, ſome in one profeſſion, ſome in another[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c109e0e2-db7c-47f7-8fc8-52406291e244",
                        "source_entry_id": "347b3608-d799-38b5-a0ab-ef94af53dd1c",
                        "source_sense_id": "6c7f9218-2585-3bb1-9829-56c0d2a0808e",
